Description: libsync's sync.h uses glibc's __BEGIN_DECLS and __END_DECLS, which musl doesn't define: defined there when missing.
Forwarded: not-needed (copium's; its author sends what fits upstream)
Origin: copium 155.2 (https://codeberg.org/selfisekai/copium: the musl patches Alpine's chromium applies), cr143-libsync-__BEGIN_DECLS.patch
The author's e-mail address is left out of the From line below.
Rebased to apply exactly (Jam OS's applier takes no fuzz): the body below is the same change made again by diff -u against this tarball.

From 4ea5b1d3b27539e8a11d7e7ef974075cf1f7e390 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LN Liberda
Date: Tue, 4 Nov 2025 14:57:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix undefined __BEGIN_DECLS define.

Not sure how this worked in the first place.
---
 include/ndk/sync.h | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/third_party/libsync/src/include/ndk/sync.h
+++ b/third_party/libsync/src/include/ndk/sync.h
@@ -31,6 +31,16 @@
 
 #include <linux/sync_file.h>
 
+#if !defined(__BEGIN_DECLS) && !defined(__END_DECLS)
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+#define __BEGIN_DECLS extern "C" {
+#define __END_DECLS }
+#else
+#define __BEGIN_DECLS
+#define __END_DECLS
+#endif
+#endif
+
 __BEGIN_DECLS
 
 /* Fences indicate the status of an asynchronous task. They are initially
